    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13476" root="دوم" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَامَآءُ</span></b>  (in the CK [erroneously] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَأْماءُ</span>) The <i>sea,</i>
or <i>a great river;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَحْرٌ</span>; (M, K;) because of
the continuance of its water: (M:) originally
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَوَمَآءُ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَوْمَآءُ</span>: if the latter, the change of the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span>
into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ا</span> is anomalous. (TA.)

